When a Spring Boot application must call 9+ third-party APIs, each with different request/response formats, the biggest mistakes are:

      Calling APIs sequentially.
      Mixing API-specific logic into business services.
      Using blocking clients (RestTemplate).
      Not implementing retries, timeouts, circuit breakers.
      Returning data only after all APIs finish.
      Not using Java 21 virtual threads or reactive processing.
======================================================================================
